al/id #uuid "272e59af-eaaf-5eb6-bcdc-320e64043c53" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755453 :tutorial/content "**MTH 256 — E1 (source title: Quiz 1)**\n\nDue: 2026-10-06\nExam date: 2026-10-06\nDate source: user-provided exam date; no submission time supplied\nDate imported: 2026-11-08\nSource: [256-E-1.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FE-1%2F256-E-1.pdf)\n\nThe complete scan preserves the student’s handwritten work. Quiz answers, worked explanations, and branch/domain corrections in this note are independently authored study additions, not an instructor key.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThe original assessment contains four problems worth 40 points and allows 40 minutes. Wait for the TA to begin and start the timer. Only a writing implement and eraser are permitted; calculators are not allowed. Complete all four problems. Problem 1 requires no supporting work. Problem 4 allows the stated variation-of-parameters alternative.\n\nStudy-link coverage is partial for distinguishing geometric integral curves from solution graphs. The vertical-line-test supporting link is outside the normal route (Test Preparation)." :tutorial/id #uuid "272e59af-eaaf-5eb6-bcdc-320e64043c53" :tutorial/title "Assignment information"}] [:tutorial/id #uuid "561cdddc-0746-5c09-a5bd-fa6e9615ed36" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755479 :tutorial/content "**MTH 256 — E2 (source title: Quiz 2)**\n\nDue: 2026-10-20\nExam date: 2026-10-20\nDate source: user-provided exam date; no submission time supplied\nDate imported: 2026-11-08\nSource: [256-E-2.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FE-2%2F256-E-2.pdf)\n\nThe complete scan preserves the student’s handwritten work. Quiz answers, worked explanations, and branch/domain corrections in this note are independently authored study additions, not an instructor key.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThe original assessment contains four problems worth 40 points and allows 40 minutes. Wait for the TA to begin and start the timer. Only a writing implement and eraser are permitted; calculators are not allowed. Complete all four problems. The source provides blank pages after Problems 1, 2, and 4 for additional work. Problem 2 requires the supplied existence-and-uniqueness theorem and explicit continuity statements.\n\nStudy-link coverage is partial for applying the existence-and-uniqueness theorem and for full branch/domain classifications. The continuity and partial-derivative links supply verified components from Multivariable Calculus, outside the normal course route." :tutorial/id #uuid "561cdddc-0746-5c09-a5bd-fa6e9615ed36" :tutorial/title "Assignment information"}] [:question/id #uuid "860969f5-95ee-5009-8088-3d650a5746b8" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1209ca3-3c8a-5bca-8709-564a7c086951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "For $x\\ne5$,\n\n$$y'=(5-x)^{-2}=\\frac1{(5-x)^2}=y^2.$$\n\nHence the function solves the ODE on each interval $(-\\infty,5)$ and $(5,\\infty)$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755547}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755547} :answer-field/id #uuid "448c417f-6b60-54c1-94fa-be922863df2a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755472}] :question/id #uuid "860969f5-95ee-5009-8088-3d650a5746b8" :question/problem "**(a)** Verify that $y=1/(5-x)$ is a solution of $y'=y^2$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed function and compare with the square of the function. The chain rule contributes two minus signs: $\\frac{d}{dx}(5-x)^{-1}=-(5-x)^{-2}(-1)$. Merely integrating or rewriting the function does not verify the equation."}] [:question/id #uuid "ab3b4840-854f-506a-b206-08b1d6d7801b" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90711706-247e-5cfc-8a84-f190bef4b691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "For any $C\\in\\mathbb R$,\n\n$$y(x)=\\ln(x^3+C),\\qquad x\\in(-\\sqrt[3]{C},\\infty).$$\n\nThese are the maximal real solution intervals; restrictions to smaller open intervals are also solutions." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755502}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755502} :answer-field/id #uuid "84404310-f19f-511a-ad6f-2e5ca2e0427c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755499}] :question/id #uuid "ab3b4840-854f-506a-b206-08b1d6d7801b" :question/problem "**(b)** Find all solutions to the equation." :question/worked-solution "Apply the natural logarithm to $e^y=x^3+C$. Its argument must be positive, so $x>\\sqrt[3]{-C}=-\\sqrt[3]{C}$. Differentiating gives $y'=3x^2/(x^3+C)=3x^2e^{-y}$. Do not put absolute values inside the logarithm: the separated relation has $e^y>0$."}] [:question/id #uuid "acc1eac8-f5a0-5e17-86a8-e3d097105f51" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755522 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10599fd1-7f2b-52d4-b3af-3f587c18857c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The guaranteed set is $\\{(x_0,y_0)\\in\\mathbb R^2:y_0\\ne0\\}$. The function $f(x,y)=(xy)^{3/5}$ is continuous everywhere, while $f_y=\\frac35x^{3/5}y^{-2/5}$ is continuous on $y\\ne0$.\n\nIf $y_0\\ne0$, choose a small open rectangle that avoids $y=0$. Both continuity hypotheses then hold. If $y_0=0$, every open rectangle contains points $(x,0)$ with $x\\ne0$, where $f_y$ does not exist, so the theorem does not guarantee uniqueness. The value $f_y(0,0)=0$ alone does not give continuity on a rectangle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755442}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755442} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2d483b5-3770-53a0-94fa-ffd571a08510" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755535}] :question/id #uuid "acc1eac8-f5a0-5e17-86a8-e3d097105f51" :question/problem "**(b)** Find every $(x_0,y_0)$ for which Theorem 2.3.1 guarantees a unique local solution. Identify $f$ and $f_y$ and their continuity sets as directed above." :question/worked-solution "A theorem's sufficient hypotheses must hold throughout a neighborhood, not merely at the initial point. In particular, $x_0=0$ does not rescue $y_0=0$. Failure of the theorem's hypotheses means no uniqueness guarantee from this theorem; it is not by itself a proof of nonuniqueness."}] [:question/id #uuid "b51e0476-b1d2-5493-9af9-bce09bc7928d" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f72e03f6-66fe-5618-8744-72a229bee71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^2-x^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755560}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755560} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b0be3d4-1da9-5424-9263-75fe204b9cbf" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755447}] :question/id #uuid "b51e0476-b1d2-5493-9af9-bce09bc7928d" :question/problem "**(a)** Find all implicit solutions.\n\nWrite the relation as {{answer}} $=C$." :question/worked-solution "On any solution interval $y\\ne0$, multiply by $y$ and integrate: $\\frac12y^2=\\frac12x^4+K$. Renaming $C=2K$ gives $y^2-x^4=C$. The ODE excludes the points with $y=0$."}] [:question/id #uuid "c9d2c3b3-447f-585e-9fe7-a34dab6205f0" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8182a2e-4a2b-5880-b28a-8336cb3ab6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln(x^3-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755527}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755527} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b12e2d1-2968-5f3a-837f-2c589aec0344" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755510}] :question/id #uuid "c9d2c3b3-447f-585e-9fe7-a34dab6205f0" :question/problem "**(c)** Solve the IVP with $y(2)=0$.\n\n$y=$ {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "Substitute into $e^y=x^3+C$: $1=8+C$, so $C=-7$. Therefore $y=\\ln(x^3-7)$ on $(\\sqrt[3]{7},\\infty)$. This interval contains $2$, and $y(2)=\\ln1=0$."}] [:question/id #uuid "e3e70ce8-9056-5f4f-98e7-69a17ba051e0" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0921f7be-2261-5c5e-82af-e49dea670fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y-x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755441}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755441} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8b408f7-c50f-5954-bcc6-4ed163d879c8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755551}] :question/id #uuid "e3e70ce8-9056-5f4f-98e7-69a17ba051e0" :question/problem "**(a)** Find all implicit solutions.\n\nWrite an equivalent relation in the form {{answer}} $=C$." :question/worked-solution "Multiply by $e^y$ and integrate: $e^y\\,dy=3x^2\\,dx$, giving $e^y=x^3+C$. Thus $e^y-x^3=C$. The relation is used where $x^3+C>0$. No equilibrium solutions are lost because $e^{-y}$ is never zero."}] [:question/id #uuid "118f3004-9f6d-5030-b2e1-7feb9d0dfce7" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755443 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e298a389-3fbe-5fed-a3d7-5e5dc64bffb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Treating $c$ as constant, $y'=(c-x)^{-2}=y^2$ for $x\\ne c$. Thus every fixed real $c$ gives solutions on intervals not crossing $x=c$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755549}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755549} :answer-field/id #uuid "981912ea-0e43-5681-9d91-71b9446f6893" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755508}] :question/id #uuid "118f3004-9f6d-5030-b2e1-7feb9d0dfce7" :question/problem "**(b)** Verify that $y=1/(c-x)$, where $c$ is a constant, is a solution of $y'=y^2$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $x$ while holding $c$ fixed. Both sides equal $1/(c-x)^2$. The singular value $x=c$ must be excluded."}] [:question/id #uuid "192392f6-44d7-504d-83c7-de78dbcd98d1" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "2c35ffba-6d7c-5e41-890b-bb9828a7254e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755456} {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "d2e8186e-1457-568a-b80a-f03fcafb4a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755539}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755539} :answer-field/id #uuid "3272277a-c801-5feb-8eb6-5a73417e96ad" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755458} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "58315aff-5a9e-545d-9c28-d8a68ccfb2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755480} {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "f991d47a-f244-5dcf-b181-f8905d71bca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755561} :answer-field/id #uuid "8416fff4-9742-5627-a1d1-88cb148d192d" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "41d1f5f5-1d3b-529a-bea6-cb90618ba1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755468} {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "c9c35956-8ef3-545c-b0d4-b8050189946d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755468} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d0eff6-a72e-5ea8-a0cb-b9dad5692ca0" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755517} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This is a graph, but it is not tangent to the field." :answer/id #uuid "36d089ac-c271-537d-99f8-7c6719688313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755459} {:answer/feedback "This is a graph, but it is not tangent to the field." :answer/id #uuid "a3632336-ef5f-5134-a554-36b9c2ae9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755516}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755516} :answer-field/id #uuid "afc76abe-6edd-52c0-8380-7bf2cc98479c" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755523} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "395f90c7-2326-5b80-ba7e-c82cd6c2eb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755463} {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "9a96a2de-3ef6-5c79-8d93-1ef05b85d96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755509}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755463} :answer-field/id #uuid "beb6b04d-ccc3-5279-95d1-3fadca02296e" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755530} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "23393cfc-4870-5b87-b5d8-cd06d38152e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755452} {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "e9f78ed6-e358-5903-aa98-b3b666ff9a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755552}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755452} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0ac7478-da95-58bb-b23d-fcb51ba4a5bd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755532}] :question/id #uuid "192392f6-44d7-504d-83c7-de78dbcd98d1" :question/problem "**(b)** Which curves are solution curves? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The indicated solution curves are $C,D,E$. They follow the field and pass the vertical line test on their regular graph portions. Curves $A$ and $B$ follow the field geometrically but fold back and do not represent single-valued functions of $x$; $F$ is not tangent to the field.\n\nThe differential equation is undefined on $y=0$ and $y=4/3$. A classical solution is considered only on an open interval where the selected graph avoids those lines; the apparent meeting point at the origin is excluded."}] [:question/id #uuid "1da7a288-d9ee-5194-a63e-449903272ed0" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755449 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0d37559-1b17-5e69-8061-902a910684b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Every $(x_0,y_0)\\in\\mathbb R^2$ qualifies for existence. Here $f(x,y)=(xy)^{3/5}$ is continuous on all of $\\mathbb R^2$: it is the composition of the continuous product $xy$, the real fifth-root function, and cubing.\n\nFor $y\\ne0$,\n\n$$f_y(x,y)=\\frac35x^{3/5}y^{-2/5}.$$\n\nThis partial derivative is continuous on the open set $y\\ne0$. At $(0,0)$ the partial derivative exists and equals $0$, but it is not continuous there. At $y=0$, $x\\ne0$, the partial derivative does not exist. Existence requires continuity of $f$ only." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755511}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755511} :answer-field/id #uuid "74f6fa68-2d14-59b5-846f-af9e5f7f0836" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755492}] :question/id #uuid "1da7a288-d9ee-5194-a63e-449903272ed0" :question/problem "**(a)** Find every $(x_0,y_0)$ for which Theorem 2.3.1 guarantees at least one local solution. Identify $f$ and $f_y$ and their continuity sets as directed above." :question/worked-solution "The odd denominator in the exponent allows negative arguments: $(xy)^{3/5}$ is real and continuous everywhere. Do not discard the axes for existence. Part (a) uses condition (a) of the theorem, not the stronger derivative condition for uniqueness."}] [:question/id #uuid "2b670c8d-3950-51c3-91b1-4d760b76f12a" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755454 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73178152-7cff-5c77-9048-7f9e20f2b8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2y^5+2y^3+y^2+3y-3x^4-3x^3-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755490}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755490} :answer-field/id #uuid "b366d2cf-3692-5f5e-a564-daeee47fb2da" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755524}] :question/id #uuid "2b670c8d-3950-51c3-91b1-4d760b76f12a" :question/problem "Source question: Problem 3, printed/PDF page 6.\n\nFind all implicit solutions of\n\n$$y'=\\frac{12x^3+9x^2+1}{10y^4+6y^2+2y+3}.$$\n\nWrite the implicit relation as {{answer}} $=C$." :question/worked-solution "Separate and integrate:\n\n$$\\int(10y^4+6y^2+2y+3)\\,dy=\\int(12x^3+9x^2+1)\\,dx,$$\n\nso $2y^5+2y^3+y^2+3y=3x^4+3x^3+x+C$. Differentiating recovers the ODE. Its denominator is positive for all real $y$, since\n\n$$10y^4+6y^2+2y+3=10y^4+6(y+1/6)^2+17/6>0.$$\n\nThus no denominator-zero values must be removed from this implicit family."}] [:question/id #uuid "30bcd75d-100a-5db4-a865-cbd5ed1332a6" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The drawn curve cuts across field segments; near x=0 its slope disagrees with the field." :answer/id #uuid "aa99e157-a46f-57c1-83b3-3c840962c4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755520} {:answer/feedback "The drawn curve cuts across field segments; near x=0 its slope disagrees with the field." :answer/id #uuid "fc2311f1-3095-5002-9ff5-ef4052f410c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755562}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755520} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cdb038-bebe-59b0-9190-4669c0db1232" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "f1545965-7182-53c9-8df6-e93a455b49a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755554} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "fcc68d23-5ac9-5b33-a2a2-d96c0a2d4497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755554} :answer-field/id #uuid "64f01a00-a97e-53ca-ae5e-c55bcf4fedf2" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "926f22f2-cf3d-5200-aa7c-c5a017e4e048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755503} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "963bbb83-b5f3-5f12-bc69-3e0dd9350840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755506}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755506} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f6d25b-110a-5e3a-a0c6-741e428c19bd" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "71f4e102-5d88-521a-a728-3ff4b0c5d94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755489} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "832f8477-af3a-5c14-b0cb-c0b6e481a477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755496}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755489} :answer-field/id #uuid "95bdb2f5-2db2-5fa0-ad7e-65b34c7deb81" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755505} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "1ae9a436-e49f-5915-8698-8c65adbed4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755446} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "8e631e52-140f-5743-9bc1-18651d6e288c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755501}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755501} :answer-field/id #uuid "973003de-94ba-5f0b-a917-b19bf781ec73" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755507} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "3d948d6c-7597-548c-9165-2289d229e024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755464} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "a15e36bf-b204-562c-9274-2ef0557c6cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755513} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc6db731-8405-5a1f-9352-bd806f5ebe83" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755563}] :question/id #uuid "30bcd75d-100a-5db4-a865-cbd5ed1332a6" :question/problem "**(a)** Which curves are integral curves? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In the source's geometric convention, $A,B,C,D,E$ are integral curves: their tangents follow the field. Curve $F$ does not.\n\nSeparating variables gives $(4y-3y^2)\\,dy=2x\\,dx$, so regular integral-curve pieces lie on levels of $2y^2-y^3-x^2=C$. Differentiating this relation recovers the ODE wherever $y\\ne0,4/3$. The displayed folds and loop are allowed for geometric integral curves; they need not each be one graph $y(x)$."}] [:question/id #uuid "37a94c9f-3744-5f95-b630-578a0901ab14" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec64d09-d570-5e6d-b0b5-91824799cbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "All real solutions are restrictions of\n\n$$y(x)=\\varepsilon\\sqrt{x^4+C},\\qquad \\varepsilon\\in\\{-1,1\\},$$\n\nwith fixed $C\\in\\mathbb R$ and fixed sign on a connected interval where $x^4+C>0$. The maximal intervals are:\n\n- $C>0$: $\\mathbb R$;\n- $C=0$: $(-\\infty,0)$ or $(0,\\infty)$;\n- $C<0$: $(-\\infty,-(-C)^{1/4})$ or $((-C)^{1/4},\\infty)$.\n\nThere is no $y=0$ solution because the equation is undefined there." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755466}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755466} :answer-field/id #uuid "01f863d5-254e-57f2-a85a-2914586a0a07" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755439}] :question/id #uuid "37a94c9f-3744-5f95-b630-578a0901ab14" :question/problem "**(b)** Find all solutions to the equation." :question/worked-solution "Solving $y^2=x^4+C$ gives both signs. Require strict positivity, because equality would give $y=0$ and make the original equation undefined. A continuous nonzero solution cannot change sign inside its interval. Differentiate either branch to check $y'=2x^3/y$."}] [:question/id #uuid "383e4acd-ffca-5f9b-8bb1-faed1d3422fa" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b37d26c-93bd-51d6-bbe3-a71409fedd93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sin x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755475}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755475} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b01d103-da11-5461-976e-6ab5689daddd" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755495}] :question/id #uuid "383e4acd-ffca-5f9b-8bb1-faed1d3422fa" :question/problem "Source question: Problem 3, PDF page 4 (10 points).\n\nSolve the initial value problem $y'=2\\cos x$, $y(0)=3$.\n\n$y=$ {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "Integration gives $y=2\\sin x+C$. At $x=0$, $3=C$, so $y=2\\sin x+3$ on $\\mathbb R$. Its derivative is $2\\cos x$ and its value at zero is $3$."}] [:question/id #uuid "42ac2f6d-24a8-5b15-bb5a-4eceb4f450ad" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755469 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b09394-fd0b-520b-9535-a70d28554758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac1{2-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755555}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755555} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef6107d-c187-588d-8ec7-9a629826351c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755467}] :question/id #uuid "42ac2f6d-24a8-5b15-bb5a-4eceb4f450ad" :question/problem "**(c)** Solve $y'=y^2$, $y(1)=1$.\n\n$y=$ {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The family in part (b) gives $1=1/(c-1)$, so $c=2$ and $y=1/(2-x)$. Its maximal interval containing $x=1$ is $(-\\infty,2)$. Check that $y'=1/(2-x)^2=y^2$ and $y(1)=1$. The equilibrium $y=0$ does not satisfy this initial condition."}] [:question/id #uuid "54cf4014-0850-58a9-9d8b-2ad541d9c8ba" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2135cc87-45da-5b27-b628-6f189d4e6687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755451} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fde169c-a4d2-5696-b7ca-978f2dfdd0e8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755484}] :question/id #uuid "54cf4014-0850-58a9-9d8b-2ad541d9c8ba" :question/problem "**(a)** Compute an integrating factor for $y'-y=e^x$.\n\n$I(x)=$ {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The standard form is $y'+P(x)y=Q(x)$ with $P(x)=-1$. Thus $I(x)=e^{\\int-1\\,dx}=e^{-x}$. Any nonzero constant multiple works; the normalized factor is shown."}] [:question/id #uuid "750cb2fa-da94-5a2c-b7de-bd011cc9d063" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614dfef7-e5ec-51a9-9691-f29fcad62f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{x^4+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755485}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755485} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b959e7-b1f1-51fb-9ec7-0a8b39fd1b5e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755558}] :question/id #uuid "750cb2fa-da94-5a2c-b7de-bd011cc9d063" :question/problem "**(c)** Solve the IVP with $y(1)=-2$.\n\n$y=$ {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "The condition gives $(-2)^2=1+C$, hence $C=3$. The negative initial value selects the negative branch: $y=-\\sqrt{x^4+3}$ on all of $\\mathbb R$. The positive branch would give $y(1)=2$ and fails the initial condition. Differentiation gives $y'=-2x^3/\\sqrt{x^4+3}=2x^3/y$."}] [:question/id #uuid "768fd77a-e15e-5446-ad16-98996572494f" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01a5bab-8e2e-5215-a946-ecbd0f28d082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+1)e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755538}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755538} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e016e55-064f-5ab2-a85d-4f3431b7ab04" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755488}] :question/id #uuid "768fd77a-e15e-5446-ad16-98996572494f" :question/problem "**(b)** Solve $y'-y=e^x$, $y(0)=1$, using the integrating-factor method or the permitted variation-of-parameters alternative.\n\n$y=$ {{answer}}." :question/worked-solution "Multiplication by $e^{-x}$ gives $(e^{-x}y)'=1$. Hence $e^{-x}y=x+C$, or $y=e^x(x+C)$. The initial condition gives $C=1$. Differentiation checks $y'-y=e^x$ on $\\mathbb R$. Notice that $xe^x+1$ would not satisfy the ODE."}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "8416fff4-9742-5627-a1d1-88cb148d192d" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "58315aff-5a9e-545d-9c28-d8a68ccfb2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755480} {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "f991d47a-f244-5dcf-b181-f8905d71bca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755561} :answer-field/id #uuid "8416fff4-9742-5627-a1d1-88cb148d192d" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755498}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "84404310-f19f-511a-ad6f-2e5ca2e0427c" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90711706-247e-5cfc-8a84-f190bef4b691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "For any $C\\in\\mathbb R$,\n\n$$y(x)=\\ln(x^3+C),\\qquad x\\in(-\\sqrt[3]{C},\\infty).$$\n\nThese are the maximal real solution intervals; restrictions to smaller open intervals are also solutions." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755502}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755502} :answer-field/id #uuid "84404310-f19f-511a-ad6f-2e5ca2e0427c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755499}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "94f6d25b-110a-5e3a-a0c6-741e428c19bd" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "926f22f2-cf3d-5200-aa7c-c5a017e4e048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755503} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "963bbb83-b5f3-5f12-bc69-3e0dd9350840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755506}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755506} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f6d25b-110a-5e3a-a0c6-741e428c19bd" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755504}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "95bdb2f5-2db2-5fa0-ad7e-65b34c7deb81" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "71f4e102-5d88-521a-a728-3ff4b0c5d94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755489} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "832f8477-af3a-5c14-b0cb-c0b6e481a477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755496}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755489} :answer-field/id #uuid "95bdb2f5-2db2-5fa0-ad7e-65b34c7deb81" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755505}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "973003de-94ba-5f0b-a917-b19bf781ec73" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "1ae9a436-e49f-5915-8698-8c65adbed4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755446} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "8e631e52-140f-5743-9bc1-18651d6e288c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755501}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755501} :answer-field/id #uuid "973003de-94ba-5f0b-a917-b19bf781ec73" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755507}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "981912ea-0e43-5681-9d91-71b9446f6893" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e298a389-3fbe-5fed-a3d7-5e5dc64bffb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Treating $c$ as constant, $y'=(c-x)^{-2}=y^2$ for $x\\ne c$. Thus every fixed real $c$ gives solutions on intervals not crossing $x=c$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755549}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755549} :answer-field/id #uuid "981912ea-0e43-5681-9d91-71b9446f6893" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755508}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "9b12e2d1-2968-5f3a-837f-2c589aec0344" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8182a2e-4a2b-5880-b28a-8336cb3ab6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln(x^3-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755527}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755527} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b12e2d1-2968-5f3a-837f-2c589aec0344" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755510}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "a6d0eff6-a72e-5ea8-a0cb-b9dad5692ca0" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "41d1f5f5-1d3b-529a-bea6-cb90618ba1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755468} {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "c9c35956-8ef3-545c-b0d4-b8050189946d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755468} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d0eff6-a72e-5ea8-a0cb-b9dad5692ca0" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755517}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "afc76abe-6edd-52c0-8380-7bf2cc98479c" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This is a graph, but it is not tangent to the field." :answer/id #uuid "36d089ac-c271-537d-99f8-7c6719688313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755459} {:answer/feedback "This is a graph, but it is not tangent to the field." :answer/id #uuid "a3632336-ef5f-5134-a554-36b9c2ae9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755516}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755516} :answer-field/id #uuid "afc76abe-6edd-52c0-8380-7bf2cc98479c" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755523}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "b366d2cf-3692-5f5e-a564-daeee47fb2da" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73178152-7cff-5c77-9048-7f9e20f2b8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2y^5+2y^3+y^2+3y-3x^4-3x^3-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755490}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755490} :answer-field/id #uuid "b366d2cf-3692-5f5e-a564-daeee47fb2da" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755524}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "beb6b04d-ccc3-5279-95d1-3fadca02296e" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "395f90c7-2326-5b80-ba7e-c82cd6c2eb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755463} {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "9a96a2de-3ef6-5c79-8d93-1ef05b85d96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755509}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755463} :answer-field/id #uuid "beb6b04d-ccc3-5279-95d1-3fadca02296e" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755530}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "c0ac7478-da95-58bb-b23d-fcb51ba4a5bd" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "23393cfc-4870-5b87-b5d8-cd06d38152e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755452} {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "e9f78ed6-e358-5903-aa98-b3b666ff9a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755552}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755452} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0ac7478-da95-58bb-b23d-fcb51ba4a5bd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755532}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "c2d483b5-3770-53a0-94fa-ffd571a08510" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10599fd1-7f2b-52d4-b3af-3f587c18857c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The guaranteed set is $\\{(x_0,y_0)\\in\\mathbb R^2:y_0\\ne0\\}$. The function $f(x,y)=(xy)^{3/5}$ is continuous everywhere, while $f_y=\\frac35x^{3/5}y^{-2/5}$ is continuous on $y\\ne0$.\n\nIf $y_0\\ne0$, choose a small open rectangle that avoids $y=0$. Both continuity hypotheses then hold. If $y_0=0$, every open rectangle contains points $(x,0)$ with $x\\ne0$, where $f_y$ does not exist, so the theorem does not guarantee uniqueness. The value $f_y(0,0)=0$ alone does not give continuity on a rectangle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755442}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755442} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2d483b5-3770-53a0-94fa-ffd571a08510" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755535}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "e8b408f7-c50f-5954-bcc6-4ed163d879c8" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0921f7be-2261-5c5e-82af-e49dea670fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y-x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755441}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755441} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8b408f7-c50f-5954-bcc6-4ed163d879c8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755551}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "f5b959e7-b1f1-51fb-9ec7-0a8b39fd1b5e" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614dfef7-e5ec-51a9-9691-f29fcad62f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{x^4+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755485}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755485} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b959e7-b1f1-51fb-9ec7-0a8b39fd1b5e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755558}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "fc6db731-8405-5a1f-9352-bd806f5ebe83" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "3d948d6c-7597-548c-9165-2289d229e024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755464} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "a15e36bf-b204-562c-9274-2ef0557c6cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755513} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc6db731-8405-5a1f-9352-bd806f5ebe83" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755563}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "01f863d5-254e-57f2-a85a-2914586a0a07" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec64d09-d570-5e6d-b0b5-91824799cbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "All real solutions are restrictions of\n\n$$y(x)=\\varepsilon\\sqrt{x^4+C},\\qquad \\varepsilon\\in\\{-1,1\\},$$\n\nwith fixed $C\\in\\mathbb R$ and fixed sign on a connected interval where $x^4+C>0$. The maximal intervals are:\n\n- $C>0$: $\\mathbb R$;\n- $C=0$: $(-\\infty,0)$ or $(0,\\infty)$;\n- $C<0$: $(-\\infty,-(-C)^{1/4})$ or $((-C)^{1/4},\\infty)$.\n\nThere is no $y=0$ solution because the equation is undefined there." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755466}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755466} :answer-field/id #uuid "01f863d5-254e-57f2-a85a-2914586a0a07" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755439}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "1b0be3d4-1da9-5424-9263-75fe204b9cbf" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f72e03f6-66fe-5618-8744-72a229bee71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^2-x^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755560}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755560} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b0be3d4-1da9-5424-9263-75fe204b9cbf" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755447}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "3272277a-c801-5feb-8eb6-5a73417e96ad" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "2c35ffba-6d7c-5e41-890b-bb9828a7254e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755456} {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "d2e8186e-1457-568a-b80a-f03fcafb4a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755539}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755539} :answer-field/id #uuid "3272277a-c801-5feb-8eb6-5a73417e96ad" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755458}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "3ef6107d-c187-588d-8ec7-9a629826351c" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b09394-fd0b-520b-9535-a70d28554758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac1{2-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755555}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755555} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef6107d-c187-588d-8ec7-9a629826351c" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755467}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "448c417f-6b60-54c1-94fa-be922863df2a" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1209ca3-3c8a-5bca-8709-564a7c086951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "For $x\\ne5$,\n\n$$y'=(5-x)^{-2}=\\frac1{(5-x)^2}=y^2.$$\n\nHence the function solves the ODE on each interval $(-\\infty,5)$ and $(5,\\infty)$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755547}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755547} :answer-field/id #uuid "448c417f-6b60-54c1-94fa-be922863df2a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755472}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "58cdb038-bebe-59b0-9190-4669c0db1232" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The drawn curve cuts across field segments; near x=0 its slope disagrees with the field." :answer/id #uuid "aa99e157-a46f-57c1-83b3-3c840962c4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755520} {:answer/feedback "The drawn curve cuts across field segments; near x=0 its slope disagrees with the field." :answer/id #uuid "fc2311f1-3095-5002-9ff5-ef4052f410c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755562}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755520} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cdb038-bebe-59b0-9190-4669c0db1232" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755481}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "5fde169c-a4d2-5696-b7ca-978f2dfdd0e8" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2135cc87-45da-5b27-b628-6f189d4e6687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755451} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fde169c-a4d2-5696-b7ca-978f2dfdd0e8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755484}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "64f01a00-a97e-53ca-ae5e-c55bcf4fedf2" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "f1545965-7182-53c9-8df6-e93a455b49a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755554} {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "fcc68d23-5ac9-5b33-a2a2-d96c0a2d4497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755554} :answer-field/id #uuid "64f01a00-a97e-53ca-ae5e-c55bcf4fedf2" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755487}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "6e016e55-064f-5ab2-a85d-4f3431b7ab04" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01a5bab-8e2e-5215-a946-ecbd0f28d082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+1)e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755538}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755538} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e016e55-064f-5ab2-a85d-4f3431b7ab04" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755488}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "74f6fa68-2d14-59b5-846f-af9e5f7f0836" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0d37559-1b17-5e69-8061-902a910684b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Every $(x_0,y_0)\\in\\mathbb R^2$ qualifies for existence. Here $f(x,y)=(xy)^{3/5}$ is continuous on all of $\\mathbb R^2$: it is the composition of the continuous product $xy$, the real fifth-root function, and cubing.\n\nFor $y\\ne0$,\n\n$$f_y(x,y)=\\frac35x^{3/5}y^{-2/5}.$$\n\nThis partial derivative is continuous on the open set $y\\ne0$. At $(0,0)$ the partial derivative exists and equals $0$, but it is not continuous there. At $y=0$, $x\\ne0$, the partial derivative does not exist. Existence requires continuity of $f$ only." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755511}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755511} :answer-field/id #uuid "74f6fa68-2d14-59b5-846f-af9e5f7f0836" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755492}] [:answer-field/id #uuid "7b01d103-da11-5461-976e-6ab5689daddd" {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b37d26c-93bd-51d6-bbe3-a71409fedd93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sin x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755475}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755475} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b01d103-da11-5461-976e-6ab5689daddd" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755495}] [:answer/id #uuid "832f8477-af3a-5c14-b0cb-c0b6e481a477" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "832f8477-af3a-5c14-b0cb-c0b6e481a477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755496}] [:answer/id #uuid "8e631e52-140f-5743-9bc1-18651d6e288c" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "8e631e52-140f-5743-9bc1-18651d6e288c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755501}] [:answer/id #uuid "90711706-247e-5cfc-8a84-f190bef4b691" {:answer/id #uuid "90711706-247e-5cfc-8a84-f190bef4b691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "For any $C\\in\\mathbb R$,\n\n$$y(x)=\\ln(x^3+C),\\qquad x\\in(-\\sqrt[3]{C},\\infty).$$\n\nThese are the maximal real solution intervals; restrictions to smaller open intervals are also solutions." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755502}] [:answer/id #uuid "926f22f2-cf3d-5200-aa7c-c5a017e4e048" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "926f22f2-cf3d-5200-aa7c-c5a017e4e048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755503}] [:answer/id #uuid "963bbb83-b5f3-5f12-bc69-3e0dd9350840" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "963bbb83-b5f3-5f12-bc69-3e0dd9350840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755506}] [:answer/id #uuid "9a96a2de-3ef6-5c79-8d93-1ef05b85d96b" {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "9a96a2de-3ef6-5c79-8d93-1ef05b85d96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755509}] [:answer/id #uuid "a0d37559-1b17-5e69-8061-902a910684b8" {:answer/id #uuid "a0d37559-1b17-5e69-8061-902a910684b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Every $(x_0,y_0)\\in\\mathbb R^2$ qualifies for existence. Here $f(x,y)=(xy)^{3/5}$ is continuous on all of $\\mathbb R^2$: it is the composition of the continuous product $xy$, the real fifth-root function, and cubing.\n\nFor $y\\ne0$,\n\n$$f_y(x,y)=\\frac35x^{3/5}y^{-2/5}.$$\n\nThis partial derivative is continuous on the open set $y\\ne0$. At $(0,0)$ the partial derivative exists and equals $0$, but it is not continuous there. At $y=0$, $x\\ne0$, the partial derivative does not exist. Existence requires continuity of $f$ only." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755511}] [:answer/id #uuid "a15e36bf-b204-562c-9274-2ef0557c6cec" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "a15e36bf-b204-562c-9274-2ef0557c6cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755513}] [:answer/id #uuid "a3632336-ef5f-5134-a554-36b9c2ae9dab" {:answer/feedback "This is a graph, but it is not tangent to the field." :answer/id #uuid "a3632336-ef5f-5134-a554-36b9c2ae9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755516}] [:answer/id #uuid "aa99e157-a46f-57c1-83b3-3c840962c4a3" {:answer/feedback "The drawn curve cuts across field segments; near x=0 its slope disagrees with the field." :answer/id #uuid "aa99e157-a46f-57c1-83b3-3c840962c4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755520}] [:answer/id #uuid "b8182a2e-4a2b-5880-b28a-8336cb3ab6b0" {:answer/id #uuid "b8182a2e-4a2b-5880-b28a-8336cb3ab6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln(x^3-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755527}] [:answer/id #uuid "c9c35956-8ef3-545c-b0d4-b8050189946d" {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "c9c35956-8ef3-545c-b0d4-b8050189946d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755536}] [:answer/id #uuid "d01a5bab-8e2e-5215-a946-ecbd0f28d082" {:answer/id #uuid "d01a5bab-8e2e-5215-a946-ecbd0f28d082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x+1)e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755538}] [:answer/id #uuid "d2e8186e-1457-568a-b80a-f03fcafb4a42" {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "d2e8186e-1457-568a-b80a-f03fcafb4a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755539}] [:answer/id #uuid "e1209ca3-3c8a-5bca-8709-564a7c086951" {:answer/id #uuid "e1209ca3-3c8a-5bca-8709-564a7c086951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "For $x\\ne5$,\n\n$$y'=(5-x)^{-2}=\\frac1{(5-x)^2}=y^2.$$\n\nHence the function solves the ODE on each interval $(-\\infty,5)$ and $(5,\\infty)$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755547}] [:answer/id #uuid "e298a389-3fbe-5fed-a3d7-5e5dc64bffb5" {:answer/id #uuid "e298a389-3fbe-5fed-a3d7-5e5dc64bffb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Treating $c$ as constant, $y'=(c-x)^{-2}=y^2$ for $x\\ne c$. Thus every fixed real $c$ gives solutions on intervals not crossing $x=c$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755549}] [:answer/id #uuid "e9f78ed6-e358-5903-aa98-b3b666ff9a59" {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "e9f78ed6-e358-5903-aa98-b3b666ff9a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755552}] [:answer/id #uuid "f1545965-7182-53c9-8df6-e93a455b49a0" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "f1545965-7182-53c9-8df6-e93a455b49a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755554}] [:answer/id #uuid "f3b09394-fd0b-520b-9535-a70d28554758" {:answer/id #uuid "f3b09394-fd0b-520b-9535-a70d28554758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac1{2-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755555}] [:answer/id #uuid "f72e03f6-66fe-5618-8744-72a229bee71e" {:answer/id #uuid "f72e03f6-66fe-5618-8744-72a229bee71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^2-x^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755560}] [:answer/id #uuid "f991d47a-f244-5dcf-b181-f8905d71bca5" {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "f991d47a-f244-5dcf-b181-f8905d71bca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755561}] [:answer/id #uuid "fc2311f1-3095-5002-9ff5-ef4052f410c1" {:answer/feedback "The drawn curve cuts across field segments; near x=0 its slope disagrees with the field." :answer/id #uuid "fc2311f1-3095-5002-9ff5-ef4052f410c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755562}] [:answer/id #uuid "fcc68d23-5ac9-5b33-a2a2-d96c0a2d4497" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "fcc68d23-5ac9-5b33-a2a2-d96c0a2d4497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755564}] [:answer/id #uuid "0921f7be-2261-5c5e-82af-e49dea670fa2" {:answer/id #uuid "0921f7be-2261-5c5e-82af-e49dea670fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y-x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755441}] [:answer/id #uuid "10599fd1-7f2b-52d4-b3af-3f587c18857c" {:answer/id #uuid "10599fd1-7f2b-52d4-b3af-3f587c18857c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The guaranteed set is $\\{(x_0,y_0)\\in\\mathbb R^2:y_0\\ne0\\}$. The function $f(x,y)=(xy)^{3/5}$ is continuous everywhere, while $f_y=\\frac35x^{3/5}y^{-2/5}$ is continuous on $y\\ne0$.\n\nIf $y_0\\ne0$, choose a small open rectangle that avoids $y=0$. Both continuity hypotheses then hold. If $y_0=0$, every open rectangle contains points $(x,0)$ with $x\\ne0$, where $f_y$ does not exist, so the theorem does not guarantee uniqueness. The value $f_y(0,0)=0$ alone does not give continuity on a rectangle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755442}] [:answer/id #uuid "1ae9a436-e49f-5915-8698-8c65adbed4d2" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." :answer/id #uuid "1ae9a436-e49f-5915-8698-8c65adbed4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755446}] [:answer/id #uuid "2135cc87-45da-5b27-b628-6f189d4e6687" {:answer/id #uuid "2135cc87-45da-5b27-b628-6f189d4e6687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755451}] [:answer/id #uuid "23393cfc-4870-5b87-b5d8-cd06d38152e0" {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "23393cfc-4870-5b87-b5d8-cd06d38152e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755452}] [:answer/id #uuid "2c35ffba-6d7c-5e41-890b-bb9828a7254e" {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "2c35ffba-6d7c-5e41-890b-bb9828a7254e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755456}] [:answer/id #uuid "36d089ac-c271-537d-99f8-7c6719688313" {:answer/feedback "This is a graph, but it is not tangent to the field." :answer/id #uuid "36d089ac-c271-537d-99f8-7c6719688313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755459}] [:answer/id #uuid "395f90c7-2326-5b80-ba7e-c82cd6c2eb76" {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "395f90c7-2326-5b80-ba7e-c82cd6c2eb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755463}] [:answer/id #uuid "3d948d6c-7597-548c-9165-2289d229e024" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "3d948d6c-7597-548c-9165-2289d229e024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755464}] [:answer/id #uuid "3ec64d09-d570-5e6d-b0b5-91824799cbb9" {:answer/id #uuid "3ec64d09-d570-5e6d-b0b5-91824799cbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "All real solutions are restrictions of\n\n$$y(x)=\\varepsilon\\sqrt{x^4+C},\\qquad \\varepsilon\\in\\{-1,1\\},$$\n\nwith fixed $C\\in\\mathbb R$ and fixed sign on a connected interval where $x^4+C>0$. The maximal intervals are:\n\n- $C>0$: $\\mathbb R$;\n- $C=0$: $(-\\infty,0)$ or $(0,\\infty)$;\n- $C<0$: $(-\\infty,-(-C)^{1/4})$ or $((-C)^{1/4},\\infty)$.\n\nThere is no $y=0$ solution because the equation is undefined there." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755466}] [:answer/id #uuid "41d1f5f5-1d3b-529a-bea6-cb90618ba1d0" {:answer/feedback "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." :answer/id #uuid "41d1f5f5-1d3b-529a-bea6-cb90618ba1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755468}] [:answer/id #uuid "4b37d26c-93bd-51d6-bbe3-a71409fedd93" {:answer/id #uuid "4b37d26c-93bd-51d6-bbe3-a71409fedd93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sin x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755475}] [:answer/id #uuid "58315aff-5a9e-545d-9c28-d8a68ccfb2d9" {:answer/feedback "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." :answer/id #uuid "58315aff-5a9e-545d-9c28-d8a68ccfb2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755480}] [:answer/id #uuid "614dfef7-e5ec-51a9-9691-f29fcad62f8f" {:answer/id #uuid "614dfef7-e5ec-51a9-9691-f29fcad62f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{x^4+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755485}] [:answer/id #uuid "71f4e102-5d88-521a-a728-3ff4b0c5d94a" {:answer/feedback "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." :answer/id #uuid "71f4e102-5d88-521a-a728-3ff4b0c5d94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755489}] [:answer/id #uuid "73178152-7cff-5c77-9048-7f9e20f2b8dd" {:answer/id #uuid "73178152-7cff-5c77-9048-7f9e20f2b8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2y^5+2y^3+y^2+3y-3x^4-3x^3-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755490}] [:multistep/id #uuid "b5487bc0-ac3f-5d8e-adc0-0b86e27c9c2f" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755526 :multistep/context "Source question: Problem 4(a–b), PDF page 5 (10 points total).\n\nThis problem assumes the integrating-factor method from lecture. If you prefer variation of parameters, you may skip part (a); in that case part (b) counts for the full 10 points." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755491} :multistep/id #uuid "b5487bc0-ac3f-5d8e-adc0-0b86e27c9c2f" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755491 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755478} :step/id #uuid "747b1567-2570-5fbc-900e-435357de9507" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755557}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755557 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755494} :step/id #uuid "f3fc6645-0135-5c84-8122-3bdf60653e1e"}]}] [:multistep/id #uuid "d8eba1be-63c4-51b6-b0f9-b648d3f5ca71" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755544 :multistep/context "Source question: Problem 2(a–b), printed/PDF page 4; page 5 is handwritten continuation.\n\nThe supplied Theorem 2.3.1 concerns $y'=f(x,y)$, $y(x_0)=y_0$:\n\n- If $f$ is continuous on an open rectangle $R=\\{(x,y):a<x<b,\\ c<y<d\\}$ containing $(x_0,y_0)$, at least one solution exists on some open subinterval of $(a,b)$ containing $x_0$.\n- If both $f$ and $f_y$ are continuous on $R$, the solution is unique on some such open subinterval.\n\nConsider\n\n$$y'=(xy)^{3/5},\\qquad y(x_0)=y_0.$$\n\nHint: $h(s)=s^{1/5}$ is continuous for every real $s$. You need not identify all rectangles. For full credit, clearly identify $f(x,y)$ and $f_y(x,y)$ and state where each is continuous." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755483} :multistep/id #uuid "d8eba1be-63c4-51b6-b0f9-b648d3f5ca71" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755483 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755449} :step/id #uuid "5e80b298-5664-5174-9030-45b48ddd5f9d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755534}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755534 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755522} :step/id #uuid "c2c1a7e4-0d36-5b0a-8af4-f9855c2fc59d"}]}] [:multistep/id #uuid "d9e11f6f-50b6-5105-b1db-1addf532f845" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755545 :multistep/context "Source question: Problem 2(a–c), PDF page 3 (4, 4, and 2 points); page 6 contains additional handwritten work." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755515} :multistep/id #uuid "d9e11f6f-50b6-5105-b1db-1addf532f845" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755515 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755500} :step/id #uuid "a32134c9-3816-5799-b758-4971eb880628" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755556}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755531 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755469} :step/id #uuid "bffee831-5f5e-5415-9897-56b368bdaf84"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755556 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755443} :step/id #uuid "f3b629de-e786-511e-ac14-5da2835248f1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755531}}]}] [:multistep/id #uuid "1f38f1bb-9bc4-55c9-b2b7-0f18fd90c546" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755450 :multistep/context "Source question: Problem 1(a–c), printed/PDF page 2; page 3 is spare workspace.\n\nConsider $y'=3e^{-y}x^2$. Hint: $\\ln(1)=0$." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755553} :multistep/id #uuid "1f38f1bb-9bc4-55c9-b2b7-0f18fd90c546" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186755444 :step/content {:db/id #ed